                <p rendition="#flush">I. <hi rendition="#italic">Report by the Deputies</hi></p>
                <p>The Ministers heard a Report on the work of the Deputies, submitted by the
                    outgoing Chairman.</p>
                <p>The Council agreed to restrict the Hydro-electric Experts’ terms of reference for
                    the Mont Cenis district to a study of the guarantees to be given by France to
                    Italy in respect to water supplies.</p>
                <p>The Experts’ terms of reference would not include a study of the hydro-electric
                    possibilities of the Mont Cenis plateau.</p>
                <p>It was agreed that the Experts’ report would be submitted to the Deputies.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">II. <hi rendition="#italic">Austro-Italian Frontier</hi></p>
                <p>After studying the Report drawn up by the Committee of Hydroelectric Experts
                    following the Austrian request for a minor rectification of the Austro-Italian
                    frontier in the north-eastern section of the Alto Adige, the Council agreed that
                    the request could not be regarded as constituting a minor frontier rectification
                    as stated in the Austrian Federal Government’s <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> of 30th May, 1946 (C.F.M. (D)
                        (46) 92).<anchor n="95" xml:id="d196-f1"/></p>
                <p>The Deputies would examine the question of the guarantees to be given to Austria
                    by Italy regarding the railway between Eastern and Northern Tyrol, through
                    Pusterthal.</p>
                <pb facs="0620" n="598" xml:id="pg598"/>
                <p rendition="#flush">III. <hi rendition="#italic">Franco-Italian Frontier</hi></p>
                <p>The Council adopted the Report of the Committee of Hydroelectric Experts for the
                    Tenda and Briga district (C.F.M.(D) (46)
                        163).<anchor n="96" xml:id="d196-f2"/> After an exchange of views the
                    Council agreed to resume consideration of the Tenda and Briga question at 5 p.m.
                    on the same afternoon.</p>
